Apply order 0001 against AxioDL/musyx 86851a3a8d51788d166ea42d137b49526f570400 (CC0-1.0; ADR 0009 section 5).
PC sndPushGroup: skip samples a group names but no directory has, as the console does
Purpose: let a group push succeed when it names samples that neither its
own sample directory nor an already resident group contains.
Console behaviour restored: on Dolphin, sndPushGroup's InsertSamples ->
ScanIDList calls dataAddSampleReference for each id and ignores a FALSE
result, so such samples are skipped and the group is pushed. The PC push
aborted the whole group instead. Mario Party 4's groups rely on the
console behaviour (group 93 names 51 such samples). Only that case is
skipped: a sample that is present but fails to upload still fails the
push. Offered upstream to AxioDL/musyx.
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/musyx/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

